{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception interface, separating motion commands from sensor events. The specification enforces safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is used in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are performed only when obstacles are detected. Recovery is conservative, with full_rotate reserved for dead-ends. The design ensures all uncontrollable events are handled in every state, and only one controllable is enabled per state to avoid oscillation.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to reflect hardware modularity.",
    "Specification automaton encodes the exploration policy: random_walk in clear, move_forward for progress, rotate_clockwise/rotate_counterclockwise for recovery, and full_rotate only as last resort."
  ],
